Vorg the Sapient wrote:

> They're chaotic.  This is consistent with elves in general, as they
> live much closer to nature than humans.  It does not mean they're
> evil; Nethack does not prescribe good and evil as alignments.  If
> lawful and chaotic simply corresponded to good and evil, then there
> wouldn't be lawful demon princes.

[ Also in reply to Jacob and Seraphim: ]

You're right. From the sources:

/* Table of all alignments */
const struct Align aligns[] = {
  {"law",     "lawful",    "Law", ROLE_LAWFUL,  A_LAWFUL},
  {"balance", "neutral",   "Neu", ROLE_NEUTRAL, A_NEUTRAL},
  {"chaos",   "chaotic",   "Cha", ROLE_CHAOTIC, A_CHAOTIC},
  {"evil",    "unaligned", "Una", 0,            A_NONE}
};

So evil *does* exist in NetHack, but good doesn't. And the demon princes
are not evil, just chaotic: only Moloch and his associates are evil.

